    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/toxotes-siamensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Toxotes siamensis, formerly known in the trade as Toxotes sp. \"Marble\", reaches up to 15–20 cm in length. It is a pure freshwater fish. It was only recently scientifically described.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/toxotes-siamensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>The species is imported from Thailand, where it inhabits the Chao Phraya river.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/toxotes-siamensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>During their research the authors found that only 2–3 of the currently 10 accepted species of archerfish are brackish water fish, while the remaining species live exclusively in freshwater.</p><p>The paper also describes two additional species of Toxotes that were previously confused with T. microlepis: Toxotes mekongensis from the Mekong (Thailand, Laos, Cambodia, Vietnam) and Toxotes sundaicus (Sumatra, Borneo, maybe Malaysia).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/toxotes-siamensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Kottelat, M. &amp; H. H. Tan (2018): Three new species of archerfishes from the freshwaters of Southeast Asia (Teleostei: Toxotidae) and notes on Henri Mouhot's fish collections. Ichthyological Exploration of Freshwaters. DOI: 10.23788/IEF-952</p>"
    }
